      "title": "Uluru - Breathable Nail Polish",
      "subtitle": "This muted redwood colored nail polish is inspired by and named after the large sandstone rock formation found in Australia. Uluru, or Ayers Rock, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and is sacred to the aboriginal people of the area. The monolith has rich indigenous history and myths and legends surrounding it that go back thousands of years. The area around the formation has ancient paintings, rock caves, springs and waterholes and is known to give off a reddish pink hue in the sunlight.\n\nUluru is a muted redwood nail polish with cool brown undertones. Uluru is more brown and less saturated than Cusco.",
